often keep a voidwalker for safety and to tank mobs while they cast spells, especially in dungeons and raids. Also because voidwalker is the only pet that can be used for "Sacrifice" shield, which is valuable in PvP and raids. So answer: Most warlocks are seen with voidwalkers because they are the default tank pet for solo and group content, provide survivability, threat, and shield, and are needed for endgame content, while succubus is more DPS/CC oriented and better for leveling but less visible in endgame.

